Subject: [PATCH 06/11] d3d10umd/d3d9, yttrium: D3D9 sampler, depth-bias, format and D32F fixes

- Keep the shader-declared sampler type while a bound texture has no pipe
  resource yet. Fixes the Heaven D3D9 abort "Unknown TGSI texture target 18"
  (F4).
- Implement D3DRS_DEPTHBIAS and D3DRS_SLOPESCALEDEPTHBIAS as unscaled
  (float) depth bias, using VK_EXT_depth_bias_control float representation,
  and disable it for points and lines as D3D9 does (F15-F16).
- Map D3DFMT_A4R4G4B4 through VK_EXT_4444_formats, D3DFMT_A8L8 with the
  luminance-alpha swizzle, and D32F_LOCKABLE to Z32_FLOAT. Bind any depth or
  stencil format as a depth-stencil resource (F15).
- Upload buffer-to-image copies into depth images through the depth aspect,
  so D32F write locks take effect; packed depth-stencil uploads stay
  rejected (F20).

Prior art: F4, F15, F16, F20 (R/VERDICT.md, R/NATIVE-WDDM20.md "D3D9 D32F"; prior-art section 2.2).
Origin: codex working tree R/mesa (git diff 374c3022), re-exported by
vmlab-win3d build/mesa; see build/mesa/README.md.
